# {{project_name}}

<!-- stacks:fill One or two sentences on what this API does and who calls it. -->

A JSON API on Django and Django REST Framework, served by gunicorn with data in SQLite, an admin for staff and a committed OpenAPI schema.

## Quickstart

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) and make.

```bash
make install
make dev          # http://127.0.0.1:8000 with reload and DEBUG on
curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/notes -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"title":"First"}'
curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/notes
```

The schema is at `/openapi.json` and in `openapi.json`. Create an admin login with `uv run python manage.py createsuperuser`, then open http://127.0.0.1:8000/admin/.

## Commands

| Command | What it does |
|---|---|
| `make dev` | Migrate, then run the development server with reload |
| `make start` | Production settings: collectstatic, migrate, then gunicorn |
| `make lint` / `make format` | Check / fix lint and formatting |
| `make typecheck` | mypy strict with the Django and DRF plugins |
| `make test` / `make coverage` | Tests, and tests with the coverage floor |
| `make makemigrations` | Write migrations after a model change |
| `make openapi` | Regenerate `openapi.json` after an API change |
| `make check-deploy` | Django's deployment checklist with production settings |

Run `make help` for the full list. Settings are environment variables; `.env.example` lists them.

## Layout

```
config/     settings, env parsing, logging, urls, wsgi, gunicorn
core/       error table and handler, API bases, request middleware, health view
accounts/   the custom user model
notes/      the example resource: model, admin, serializer, viewset, routes
tests/      API tests through DRF's test client
docs/       architecture, HTTP contract, development
```

